# Repo-root .dockerignore - only relevant to backend/Dockerfile.render,
# the single Render-consolidated build whose context is the repo root (it
# needs access to both backend/ and frontend/ to bundle the frontend into
# the backend image). docker-compose.yml's backend/frontend services keep
# their own per-directory build contexts and .dockerignore files unchanged.
**/node_modules
# Broad on purpose - catches any current or future dotenv-style secret file
# regardless of naming (the previous **/.env / **/.env.local / **/.env.*.local
# trio missed e.g. root .env.notion, which doesn't end in .local). Nothing in
# Dockerfile.render's COPY steps needs any .env* file, including .example
# ones, so no re-include is needed.
**/.env*
mobile
frontend/dist
frontend/tests
frontend/coverage
backend/uploads
backend/logs
backend/coverage
backend/tests
.git
*.md
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
*.swp
*.swo
*~
